+      "environment": "docker",
+      "version": "latest",
+      "solution": "Wrote the runbook to **`~/systemd-restart-always-deleted-inode-fix.md`**.\n\n## What I verified empirically\nSince no repo is present, I reproduced the exact inode mechanism in the sandbox (`/proc/<pid>/exe` + hash proof):\n\n- Built `svcdemo` **v1** → started it (`Restart=always` proxy).\n- Rebuilt the same path to **v2**: disk hash changed, `/proc/75/exe -> ... (deleted)`, and the **running process still printed `VERSION=v1-old`** while disk was `v2-new`.\n- Killed MainPID and relaunched: link is clean, hashes equal, and it prints `VERSION=v2-new`.\n\n## Root cause (the part the existing gate misses)\n- In-place builds publish a **new inode**; the running process keeps the old one, rendered as ` (deleted)` by the kernel.\n- `Restart=always` is **exit-triggered** — a successful rebuild never signals the process, so it serves the dead inode indefinitely.\n- `check-binary-fresh` only diffs **source tree vs. built file on disk** (both new) → green. It never hashes `/proc/<MainPID>/exe`.\n- Stale `gitreins/tasks.yaml` keeps the tree dirty, so the version-stamped target skips/refuses the new stamp — clean the tree first.\n\n## Core fix\n```\ngit restore --source=HEAD --staged --worktree gitreins/tasks.yaml   # clean dirty stamp\nmake build VERSION=\"$(git describe --tags --always --dirty)\"        # stamped artifact\nsystemctl restart \"$UNIT\"                                           # or kill MainPID (Restart=always)\n```\nThen verify `readlink /proc/<newPID>/exe` has no ` (deleted)`, `sha256` running image == disk artifact, `/version` shows the new describe, and `make check-deploy` leg 3 + `make tick-closeout` pass.\n\nThe doc also includes the diagnosis command set, a one-shot remediation script, the missing **leg-3 running-image gate** to install, and a prevention checklist.\n",
+      "evidence": "# Evidence\n- Problem class: systemd-restart-always-deleted-inode-artifact-deploy-drift\n- Model: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\n- Solved: 2026-10-28T19:38:00.163Z\n- Verification: solution produced by pi in sandbox; see signatures.json\n",
+      "signatures": {
+        "description": "A systemd unit with Restart=always keeps executing a superseded binary after an in-place rebuild: /proc/<MainPID>/exe points at /path/binary (deleted) and the running process serves the OLD code version, while disk artifact-freshness checks that diff source-vs-built-file read green (data-only drift tolerated). Diagnosis oracle: /proc/<pid>/exe showing \" (deleted)\" suffix = the running image is a deleted inode, not the current artifact; systemd systemctl show -p MainPID -p ExecMainStartTimestamp gives the serving start time to compare against the fix commit time. Remedy: make the tree clean (stale gitreins/tasks.yaml dirty-stamps builds), rebuild with the version-stamped target, then kill the MainPID so Restart=always relaunches on the live artifact; verify via /proc/<newpid>/exe (no deleted suffix) + live version endpoint + the repo close-out gate (e.g. make check-deploy leg 3 / tick-closeout) which fails leg 3 exactly on this shape. Evidence: tick 492 of off-by-one 2026-10-28 — PID 988251 served v0.2.0-104-g8a5648f3 (deleted inode) for ~16h while check-binary-fresh PASSed and only check-deploy leg 3 + tick-closeout (rc=2) caught it; post-remedy PID 1968856 serves v0.2.0-130-g151e8de3 with all gates PASS.",
