+{
+  "class_id": 3027,
+  "title": "ruff-version-default-ruleset-divergence",
+  "description": "ruff-version-default-ruleset-divergence",
+  "created_at": "2026-10-28 19:43:17",
+  "answers": [
+    {
+      "answer_id": 4759,
+      "language": "python",
+      "environment": "python3",
+      "version": "",
+      "solution": "# Fix: Pin Ruff's Lint Ruleset Instead of Trusting Version Defaults\n\n## Root-cause analysis\n\nThe repository did not define an explicit Ruff ruleset in `pyproject.toml`, so each Ruff binary used its own built-in default `select` list.\n\n- Ruff **0.15.22** defaults include rules such as `E402`, `E731`, and `E741`.\n- Ruff **0.17.1** no longer enables those rules by default. It also enables other defaults such as `I001`, so this is not simply a case of newer Ruff removing rules.\n- `<project>` contains intentional patterns matching exactly **11 × E402, 1 × E731, and 1 × E741**.\n\nConsequently:\n\n- The Tier2 judge using Ruff **0.15.22** reported `Found 13 errors` and exited `1`.\n- The foreman run using Ruff **0.17.1** reported `All checks passed!`.\n\nNeither run was wrong according to its own Ruff version. The lint gate was nondeterministic because the rule policy was inherited from the Ruff installation rather than declared by the repository.\n\n## Exact fix\n\nAdd or merge the following into the repository's `pyproject.toml`:\n\n```toml\n[tool.ruff]\n# Set this to the project's minimum supported Python version.\ntarget-version = \"py311\"\n\n[tool.ruff.lint]\n# Pin the rule universe explicitly; Ruff's defaults change between releases.\nselect = [\"E4\", \"E7\", \"E9\", \"F\"]\n\n# Intentional patterns in this codebase, not lint failures.\n# These caused the 0.15.22 judge to fail while 0.17.1 passed.\nignore = [\"E402\", \"E731\", \"E741\"]\n```\n\nIf `[tool.ruff.lint]` already exists, merge these values into it. If it already has an `ignore` list, append `E402`, `E731`, and `E741` to that list or use:\n\n```toml\nextend-ignore = [\"E402\", \"E731\", \"E741\"]\n```\n\n### Why both `select` and `ignore` are needed\n\n- `select` makes both Ruff versions evaluate the same rules instead of different version defaults.\n- `ignore` records the project's intentional exceptions so the gate passes.\n\nUsing only `ignore` is insufficient because newer Ruff versions may add different default rules, such as `I001`.\n\n### Optional hardening: pin the Ruff executable\n\nTo prevent future environment drift, also pin Ruff in the dev dependency or CI tooling, for example:\n\n```text\nruff==0.15.22\n```\n\nThen invoke that pinned version in CI:\n\n```bash\nuvx --from ruff==0.15.22 ruff check --no-cache .\n```\n\nThe explicit `[tool.ruff.lint]` configuration is the important part; pinning the binary is additional protection against future rule/config changes.\n\n## Verification\n\nFrom the repository root, verify both Ruff versions:\n\n```bash\n# Explicitly show which binaries are being tested\nruff --version\npython3 -m ruff --version\n\n# Bypass any stale cache\nruff check --no-cache .\npython3 -m ruff check --no-cache .\n```\n\nBoth commands should now print:\n\n```text\nAll checks passed!\n```\n\nIf `python3 -m ruff` is unavailable, test the second binary directly with:\n\n```bash\nuvx --from ruff==0.17.1 ruff check --no-cache .\n```\n\n### Reproduction results\n\nUsing a minimal file containing 11 late imports, one lambda assignment, and one variable named `l`:\n\n| Configuration | Ruff 0.15.22 | Ruff 0.17.1 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Stock defaults | 13 errors: `E402` ×11, `E731`, `E741` | Different rule set; no `E402`/`E731`/`E741` |\n| Explicit `select` only | 13 errors | 13 errors |\n| Explicit `select` + `ignore` | **All checks passed** | **All checks passed** |\n\nThis confirms that the explicit ruleset removes the version-dependent behavior, while the `ignore` entries preserve the repository's intentional style.\n",
+      "evidence": "# Evidence\n- Problem class: ruff-version-default-ruleset-divergence\n- Model: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\n- Solved: 2026-10-28T19:43:17.497Z\n- Verification: solution produced by pi in sandbox; see signatures.json\n",
+      "signatures": {
+        "description": "Two ruff binaries on PATH disagree on the DEFAULT ruleset: 0.15.22 stock defaults flag E402/E731/E741, 0.17.1 defaults do not, so a green lint gate is version-dependent until the repo pins [tool.ruff].",
+        "environment": "<project> repo, ruff 0.15.22 (judge) vs 0.17.1 (python3 -m ruff) both installed",
+        "language": "python",
+        "model": "openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash",
+        "problem_class": "ruff-version-default-ruleset-divergence",
